\subsubsection{Lagrangian reward channel and dual ascent}\label{sec:method:lag}

Each step logs \(\big(q_k,\texttt{rebuffer}_k,\mathrm{smooth}_k,\phi(B_k),\psi^{\mathrm{Lya}}_k\big)\) into \texttt{info}; \(\widetilde{\mathrm{RB}}_k,\widetilde{\mathrm{SM}}_k\) match the stall/smooth penalties in~\eqref{eq:L}.
The PPO surrogate uses (repository scaling \(1/100\) for SB3 numerics)
\begin{equation}
\label{eq:rtrain}
    r^{\mathrm{train}}_k
    = \frac{1}{100}\Big(
        q_k
        - \lambda_r \,\widetilde{\mathrm{RB}}_k
        - \lambda_s \,\widetilde{\mathrm{SM}}_k
        - w_b\,\phi(B_k)
        - w_\ell\,\psi^{\mathrm{Lya}}_k
    \Big).
\end{equation}
After a warm-up phase (\(H{=}60\) episodes), episodic \(\hat{\mathrm{RB}},\hat{\mathrm{SM}}\) drive asymmetric projected dual ascent on gaps \(g_r=\hat{\mathrm{RB}}-\delta_{\mathrm{rf}}\), \(g_s=\hat{\mathrm{SM}}-\delta_{\mathrm{sm}}\) with caps \([\lambda^{\min},\lambda^{\max}]\) per axis~\cite{paternain2019dual,tian2022towards}; vectorized workers share the current \(\lambda_{\bullet}\) values.

\subsection{Catastrophic risk detection and pessimistic feasibility}\label{sec:method:risk}

The shields never learn parameters; each evaluates \textbf{deterministic} predicates on manifest data and a conservative kbps estimate.
Let \(\overline{\mathrm{tp}}_k\) be the instantaneous trace throughput at chunk \(k\) and \(\underline{C}_k\) the \emph{pessimistic} kbps estimate
\begin{equation}
\label{eq:tp-pessimistic}
    \underline{C}_k
    = \max\!\Big\{C_{\min},\ \rho \cdot \min\{\overline{\mathrm{tp}}_k,\mathrm{last\_tp}_k\}\Big\},
\end{equation}
with pessimism \(\rho\in(0,1]\) and an emulator throughput floor \(C_{\min}\).
Default values are \(\rho{=}0.97\) for training and \(\rho{=}0.90\) for the VMAF-aware sweep reported in Section~\ref{sec:eval}.
For candidate representation \(j\), predicted download seconds are
\begin{equation}
\label{eq:dest}
    d^{\mathrm{est}}_k(j)
    = \min\!\left\{\frac{\sigma_k(j)}{\underline{C}_k\cdot 10^{3}},\ 60\right\},
\end{equation}
where \(\sigma_k(j)\) is manifest chunk size in bits for bitrate index \(j\) at chunk \(k\).
A fluid analogue of post-download buffer (ignoring simultaneous playback credit during download, but mirroring conservative tests) is
\begin{equation}
\label{eq:btilde}
    \widetilde{B}_{k+1}(j)=\max\{0,\,B_k-d^{\mathrm{est}}_k(j)\}+T_{\mathrm{c}},
\end{equation}
which operators can compare against a \textbf{safety floor} \(B_{\mathrm{safe}}\): if \(\widetilde{B}_{k+1}(j)\) is routinely below \(B_{\mathrm{safe}}\), representation \(j\) is emergency-infeasible.
\textbf{Risk gate.} When enabled, the shield \emph{passes through} \(a^{\mathrm{raw}}_k\) whenever
\begin{equation}
\label{eq:risk-gate}
    d^{\mathrm{est}}_k(a^{\mathrm{raw}}_k)\le \max\{B_k,0.1\}\cdot\rho_{\mathrm{risk}},
\end{equation}
with \(\rho_{\mathrm{risk}}{=}1.35\) as default; benign proposals therefore skip projection~\cite{alshiekh2018shielding}.
\textbf{Catastrophic pass-through.} In the VMAF-aware path, if \(d^{\mathrm{est}}_k(a^{\mathrm{raw}}_k)\le B_k\,\rho_{\mathrm{cat}}\) the shield returns \(a^{\mathrm{exec}}_k=a^{\mathrm{raw}}_k\) without constructing the VMAF candidate pool (Algorithm~\ref{alg:shield-vmaf}).
The \texttt{light} mode uses the same inequality as a fast no-intervention check before margin-based repair.
\textbf{Critical buffer.} If \(B_k\le B_{\mathrm{crit}}\) (default \(0.20\)--\(0.30\)~s), the shield snaps to the lowest index \(0\) as a hard emergency rule.

\subsection{Deterministic runtime projection}\label{sec:method:shield}

\textbf{Role.} \(\mathcal{S}:(s_k,a^{\mathrm{raw}}_k)\mapsto(a^{\mathrm{exec}}_k,\iota_k)\) executes \emph{before} \texttt{env.step}; \(\iota_k\in\{0,1\}\) logs interventions for audit CSVs (Section~\ref{sec:eval}).

\subsubsection{QoE-oriented shield core}\label{sec:method:shield:v13}

Besides \texttt{off}, the shield exposes three operating modes: \texttt{qoe}, \texttt{light}, and \texttt{strong}.
All modes share \(\underline{C}_k\) and \(d^{\mathrm{est}}_k(\cdot)\) from~\eqref{eq:tp-pessimistic}--\eqref{eq:dest}, clip \(a^{\mathrm{raw}}_k\) to \(\mathcal{B}\), apply the critical-buffer snap, and honor the optional risk gate~\eqref{eq:risk-gate}.
The \texttt{qoe} mode searches downward from \(a^{\mathrm{raw}}_k\) over at most \(\Delta_{\mathrm{dn}}\) index steps (default \(2\)), but \emph{accepts} representations whose predicted download fits a small \textbf{predicted-stall budget} \(\zeta\) (default \(0.25\)~s), i.e.\ \(d^{\mathrm{est}}_k(j)\le B_k+\zeta\), before widening search down to a minimum guard index \(j_{\min}\) (default \(1\)).
If no candidate satisfies the budget, the shield may emit an emergency index~\(0\) when the minimum guard index \(j_{\min}\) would imply a predicted stall above threshold~\(\xi\) (default \(1.25\)~s); otherwise it returns \(j_{\min}\).
The \texttt{light} and \texttt{strong} modes apply buffer-margin feasibility tests with defaults \(\rho_{\mathrm{cat}}{=}2.50\), \(\mu_{\ell}{=}0.15\)~s, \(\mu_s{=}0.75\)~s.
Algorithm~\ref{alg:shield-v13} details the full procedure; the shield wrapper may additionally cap post-intervention upshifts during a short recovery window.

\begin{algorithm}[t]
\caption{QoE-oriented shield core}
\label{alg:shield-v13}
\begin{algorithmic}[1]
\STATE \textbf{Input:} \(a^{\mathrm{raw}}\), buffer \(B_k\), chunk \(k\), trace + \texttt{last\_tp}, \(\sigma_k(\cdot)\); cfg \((\texttt{level},B_{\mathrm{crit}},j_{\min},\rho,\rho_{\mathrm{risk}},\rho_{\mathrm{cat}},\Delta_{\mathrm{dn}},\zeta,\xi,\mu_{\ell},\mu_s,\texttt{risk\_on},\texttt{emergency})\)
\STATE \(a\leftarrow \mathrm{clip}(a^{\mathrm{raw}},0,L{-}1)\); compute \(\underline{C}_k\), \(d^{\mathrm{est}}_k(\cdot)\) via~\eqref{eq:tp-pessimistic}--\eqref{eq:dest}
\IF{\(\texttt{level}=\texttt{off}\)} \STATE \textbf{return} \((a,\,0)\) \ENDIF
\IF{\(B_k\le B_{\mathrm{crit}}\)}
    \IF{\(a=0\)} \STATE \textbf{return} \((0,\,0)\) \ELSE \STATE \textbf{return} \((0,\,1)\) \ENDIF
\ENDIF
\IF{\texttt{risk\_on} \textbf{and} \(d^{\mathrm{est}}_k(a)\le \max\{B_k,0.1\}\,\rho_{\mathrm{risk}}\)} \STATE \textbf{return} \((a,\,0)\) \ENDIF
\IF{\(\texttt{level}=\texttt{qoe}\)}
    \STATE \(f\leftarrow \max\{j_{\min},\,a-\Delta_{\mathrm{dn}}\}\)
    \FOR{\(c=a,a-1,\ldots,f\)}
        \IF{\(d^{\mathrm{est}}_k(c)\le B_k+\zeta\)}
            \IF{\(c=a\)} \STATE \textbf{return} \((c,\,0)\) \ELSE \STATE \textbf{return} \((c,\,1)\) \ENDIF
        \ENDIF
    \ENDFOR
    \FOR{\(c=f-1,f-2,\ldots,j_{\min}\)}
        \IF{\(d^{\mathrm{est}}_k(c)\le B_k+\zeta\)}
            \IF{\(c=a\)} \STATE \textbf{return} \((c,\,0)\) \ELSE \STATE \textbf{return} \((c,\,1)\) \ENDIF
        \ENDIF
    \ENDFOR
    \IF{\texttt{emergency} \textbf{and} \(j_{\min}>0\) \textbf{and} \(\max\{0,\,d^{\mathrm{est}}_k(j_{\min})-B_k\}>\xi\)}
        \IF{\(a=0\)} \STATE \textbf{return} \((0,\,0)\) \ELSE \STATE \textbf{return} \((0,\,1)\) \ENDIF
    \ENDIF
    \IF{\(a=j_{\min}\)} \STATE \textbf{return} \((j_{\min},\,0)\) \ELSE \STATE \textbf{return} \((j_{\min},\,1)\) \ENDIF
\ENDIF
\IF{\(\texttt{level}=\texttt{light}\)}
    \IF{\(d^{\mathrm{est}}_k(a)\le B_k\,\rho_{\mathrm{cat}}\)} \STATE \textbf{return} \((a,\,0)\) \ENDIF
    \FOR{\(c=a-1,a-2,\ldots,j_{\min}\)}
        \IF{\(d^{\mathrm{est}}_k(c)\le \max\{B_k-\mu_{\ell},\,0\}\)} \STATE \textbf{return} \((c,\,1)\) \ENDIF
    \ENDFOR
    \IF{\(a=j_{\min}\)} \STATE \textbf{return} \((j_{\min},\,0)\) \ELSE \STATE \textbf{return} \((j_{\min},\,1)\) \ENDIF
\ENDIF
\STATE \(c\leftarrow a\)
\WHILE{\(c>j_{\min}\) \textbf{and} \(d^{\mathrm{est}}_k(c)>\max\{B_k-\mu_s,\,0\}\)}
    \STATE \(c\leftarrow c-1\)
\ENDWHILE
\IF{\(c=a\)} \STATE \textbf{return} \((c,\,0)\) \ELSE \STATE \textbf{return} \((c,\,1)\) \ENDIF
\end{algorithmic}
\end{algorithm}

\subsubsection{VMAF-aware perceptual projection}\label{sec:method:shield:v12}

\textbf{Legacy path.} Without VMAF awareness, the \texttt{light} and \texttt{strong} modes perform index-decrement search with margins \(\mu\).
\textbf{VMAF-aware path.}
Define the soft-safe candidate set (never upswitching)
\begin{equation}
\label{eq:softsafe}
    \mathcal{J}_k
    = \Big\{\, j\in\mathcal{B}:\ j\le a^{\mathrm{raw}}_k,\ \ d^{\mathrm{est}}_k(j)\le B_k\,\sigma_{\mathrm{soft}}\,\Big\},
\end{equation}
where \(\sigma_{\mathrm{soft}}\) (\texttt{soft\_tolerance}) relaxes the hard buffer equality into a tunable slack band.
Let \(V_k(j)\) be manifest VMAF for index \(j\) at chunk \(k\) (monotone proxy if missing).
Among candidates whose perceptual loss vs.\ the proposal stays within budget \(\tau\) (\texttt{vmaf\_loss\_budget}),
\begin{equation}
    \mathcal{J}'_k = \Big\{\, j\in\mathcal{J}_k:\ V_k(a^{\mathrm{raw}}_k)-V_k(j)\le \tau\,\Big\},
\end{equation}
pick \(\mathcal{J}^\star_k=\mathcal{J}'_k\) if non-empty, otherwise \(\mathcal{J}^\star_k=\mathcal{J}_k\).
The implementation returns
\begin{equation}
    a^{\mathrm{exec}}_k = \arg\max_{j\in\mathcal{J}^\star_k} \Big( V_k(j),\ j,\ -d^{\mathrm{est}}_k(j) \Big),
\end{equation}
i.e.\ maximize VMAF, break ties toward the higher index, then shorter predicted download (lexicographic tie-breaking).
If \(\mathcal{J}_k=\emptyset\), the shield falls back to index \(0\).
\textbf{Lookahead gate (optional).} When a lookahead horizon $H>0$ is configured, a short pessimistic rollout under the raw action can bypass projection if buffers never dip below a minimum threshold; this gate is evaluated \emph{before} the VMAF-aware branch.

\textbf{Design-space remark.} Sweeps over \(\VShieldVariants\) configurations collapse to \(\VShieldBehaviors\) behavioral classes dominated by whether VMAF-aware fallback is enabled (Section~\ref{sec:eval:shields}).

\begin{algorithm}[t]
\caption{VMAF-aware perceptual projection}
\label{alg:shield-vmaf}
\begin{algorithmic}[1]
\STATE \textbf{Input:} raw index \(a^{\mathrm{raw}}\), buffer \(B_k\), chunk \(k\), trace + last throughput, bits \(\sigma_k(\cdot)\), VMAF table \(\{V_k(j)\}_{j\in\mathcal{B}}\), \((\rho,\rho_{\mathrm{cat}},\rho_{\mathrm{risk}},\sigma_{\mathrm{soft}},\tau,B_{\mathrm{crit}})\) (after optional lookahead gate)
\STATE \(a\leftarrow \mathrm{clip}(a^{\mathrm{raw}},0,L{-}1)\); compute \(\underline{C}_k\) by~\eqref{eq:tp-pessimistic}; \(\forall j:\ d^{\mathrm{est}}_k(j)\) by~\eqref{eq:dest}
\IF{\(B_k\le B_{\mathrm{crit}}\)}
    \IF{\(a=0\)} \STATE \textbf{return} \((0,\,0)\) \ELSE \STATE \textbf{return} \((0,\,1)\) \ENDIF
\ENDIF
\IF{risk gate enabled \textbf{and} \(d^{\mathrm{est}}_k(a)\le \max\{B_k,0.1\}\rho_{\mathrm{risk}}\)}
    \STATE \textbf{return} \((a,\,0)\)
\ENDIF
\IF{\textbf{not} VMAF-aware mode}
    \STATE apply legacy light/strong index projection; \textbf{return}
\ENDIF
\IF{\(d^{\mathrm{est}}_k(a)\le B_k\,\rho_{\mathrm{cat}}\)}
    \STATE \textbf{return} \((a,\,0)\)
\ENDIF
\STATE build \(\mathcal{J}_k\) per~\eqref{eq:softsafe}
\IF{\(\mathcal{J}_k=\emptyset\)}
    \IF{\(a=0\)} \STATE \textbf{return} \((0,\,0)\) \ELSE \STATE \textbf{return} \((0,\,1)\) \ENDIF
\ENDIF
\STATE \(\mathcal{J}'_k\leftarrow\{j\in\mathcal{J}_k:\ V_k(a)-V_k(j)\le\tau\}\); \(\mathcal{J}^\star_k\leftarrow \mathcal{J}'_k\) if non-empty else \(\mathcal{J}_k\)
\STATE \(a^{\mathrm{exec}}\leftarrow \arg\max_{j\in\mathcal{J}^\star_k} (V_k(j),\ j,\ -d^{\mathrm{est}}_k(j))\) (lexicographic)
\IF{\(a^{\mathrm{exec}}=a\)} \STATE \textbf{return} \((a^{\mathrm{exec}},0)\) \ELSE \STATE \textbf{return} \((a^{\mathrm{exec}},1)\) \ENDIF
\end{algorithmic}
\end{algorithm}

\subsection{Optional shield-aware shaping and hysteresis}

A shield-aware penalty wrapper penalizes shield interventions: \(\beta_{\mathrm{sh}}\iota_k+\gamma_{\mathrm{sh}}|a^{\mathrm{exec}}_k-a^{\mathrm{raw}}_k|\) with \(\beta_{\mathrm{sh}}{=}0.08,\gamma_{\mathrm{sh}}{=}0.03\).
A hysteresis wrapper caps index swings and blocks upswitches when \(B_k<1.5\)~s.
The shield wrapper optionally applies smooth-recovery upshift caps after interventions.

\subsection{End-to-end training loop (primal--dual PPO + optional shield)}

Algorithm~\ref{alg:train} composes wrappers with SB3-PPO; Table~\ref{tab:hypers} freezes hyper-parameters.

\begin{algorithm}[t]
\caption{Lagrangian PPO training with optional shield-at-train}
\label{alg:train}
\begin{algorithmic}[1]
\STATE Instantiate vectorized SB3-PPO\((\theta)\); wrap envs with \texttt{LagrangianRewardWrapper} lineage and optional hysteresis / \texttt{ShieldAwarePenalty}.
\FOR{optimization iteration until budget}
    \FOR{parallel worker \(w\)}
        \STATE Reset env; load shared \((\lambda_r,\lambda_s)\) per artifact.
        \FOR{environment step \(k{=}1{:}K_e\)}
            \STATE \(a^{\mathrm{raw}}_k\sim\pi_\theta(\cdot\mid s_k)\)
            \STATE \(a^{\mathrm{exec}}_k \gets \mathcal{S}(s_k,a^{\mathrm{raw}}_k)\) if shield wraps training env, else \(a^{\mathrm{raw}}_k\)
            \STATE Step emulator with \(a^{\mathrm{exec}}_k\); log \(\{q_k,\widetilde{\mathrm{RB}}_k,\widetilde{\mathrm{SM}}_k,\phi,\psi^{\mathrm{Lya}}\}\)
            \STATE \(r^{\mathrm{train}}_k \gets\) Eq.~\eqref{eq:rtrain} plus optional shield-aware shaping
        \ENDFOR
        \STATE Episode end: update moving averages of \(\hat{\mathrm{RB}},\hat{\mathrm{SM}}\); if past warm-up \(\Rightarrow\) projected dual ascent \(\Pi_{\Lambda}\)
        \STATE Push transitions into PPO rollout buffer
    \ENDFOR
    \STATE PPO.update() (GAE + clipped surrogate + entropy)
\ENDFOR
\end{algorithmic}
\end{algorithm}

\subsection{Policy--shield co-design strategy}\label{sec:method:codesign}

Lagrangian PPO enforces CMDP budgets only in \textbf{expectation} over rollouts: \(\lambda_r,\lambda_s\) chase \(\delta_{\mathrm{rf}},\delta_{\mathrm{sm}}\), but the neural map \(\pi_\theta\) can still propose aggressive representations on single steps---especially under 5G/mmWave draws outside the training mixture~\cite{meng2024mmwave,paternain2019dual}.
The shield is the complementary \textbf{deterministic safety net}: it never replaces \(\pi_\theta\)'s representational capacity, but repairs individual proposals before they hit the plant~\cite{alshiekh2018shielding}.
\textbf{Co-design.} When shields wrap training, \(\pi_\theta\) learns to rely on this safety net: the QoE-oriented guard (Algorithm~\ref{alg:shield-v13}) pairs with Lagrangian PPO during training, while the VMAF-aware perceptual projection (Algorithm~\ref{alg:shield-vmaf}) trims catastrophic downloads under explicit VMAF budgets at inference~\cite{li2016vmaf}.
Removing the shield at inference breaks the implicit contract, inflating rebuffering (Section~\ref{sec:eval:codesign}); the observed Pareto improvement is a property of the \emph{joint} system (Lagrangian PPO + deterministic shield), not of either module in isolation.
We recommend shipping the same shield configuration used in training and tuning perceptual knobs (\(\tau\), \(\rho_{\mathrm{cat}}\), \(\zeta\), \(\rho_{\mathrm{risk}}\)) rather than disabling guards.

\subsection{Implementation Notes and Hyperparameters}

The implementation ships as Lagrangian reward wrappers plus deterministic shield modules.
